Extracted Text & Field Mapping
Section 1: Definition
 * Text: In this Schedule, "the Regulations" means the Immigration Regulations, 2014, published under Government Notice No. R. 413 of 22 May 2014, as amended by Government Notice No. R. 1328 of 29 November 2018.
Section 2: Amendment of regulation 1 of Regulations
 * Text:
   * (a) Substitution for definition of "police clearance certificate":
     > "police clearance certificate" means a certificate issued, in respect of criminal records or the character of an applicant, by the police or competent authority in each country where an applicant, after having attained the age of 18 years, resided for 12 months or longer during the five years immediately preceding the date of application, which certificate shall not be older than six months at the time of submission: Provided that in the case of a renewal or extension of a visa, such a certificate shall be issued by the South African Police Service or competent authority of the Republic;
     > 
   * (b) Deletion of definition of "radiological report".
Section 3: Amendment of regulation 9 of Regulations
 * Text:
   * (a) Subregulation (1)(c) substituted:
     > "(c) a medical report in respect of each applicant, excluding applicants for the visa contemplated in section 11(1)(a) of the Act;"
     > 
   * (b) Subregulation (9)(a) addition of sub-paragraphs:
     > "(iii) is the spouse or child of a South African citizen or permanent resident;"
     > "(iv) is the parent of a citizen or permanent resident child;"
     > 
Section 4: Amendment of regulation 11 of Regulations
 * Text: Subregulation (4) substituted:
   * Activities contemplated in section 11(1)(b)(iv) of the Act:
     * (a) Work conducted for foreign employer (international school teaching, film/advertising workers [actor, cameraman, hairstylist, makeup artist, lighting/sound engineer], foreign journalist seconded, visiting professor/lecturer/researcher, artist writing/painting/sculpting, entertainment industry worker in transit, tour leader/host, religious leader).
     * (b) Remote work for foreign employer / foreign source income:
       * (i) Gross income no less than equivalent of R1,000,000.00 per annum.
       * (ii) Visa ≤ 6 months within 36-month period: may apply to SARS for tax registration exemption.
       * (iii) Visa > 6 months within 36-month period: must register with SARS.
       * (iv) Complies with SA employment legislation where applicable.
     * (c) Accompanying visa holder (sections 11, 13, 14, 15, 17, 18, 19, 20 or 22) as spouse/child.
     * (d) Testifying as state witness in criminal court case (initiated by Deputy Director of Public Prosecutions).
Section 5: Amendment of regulation 18 of Regulations
 * Text:
   * (a) Subregulation (5)(b) substitution: Professional body registration proof SAQA recognized under NQF Act section 13(1)(i). Application proof = max 12 months visa; Certificate proof = full period under subregulation (6).
   * (b) Insertion of subregulations (12) and (13):
     * (12) Points-based system determined by Minister by notice in Gazette for section 19 work visas.
     * (13) Factors considered: (a) age, (b) qualifications, (c) language skills, (d) work experience, (e) offer of employment, (f) salary, (g) any other relevant factor.
Section 6: Amendment of regulation 20 of Regulations
 * Text: Subregulation (9)(h) substituted: SAQA professional body registration proof for corporate visa.
Section 7: Amendment of regulation 23 of Regulations
 * Text: Subregulation (2)(f) substituted with "(f) a medical report;".
Section 8: Amendment of regulation 24 of Regulations
 * Text: Subregulations (5)(d) & (6)(c) substituted regarding SAQA professional body registration proof for business visa.
Section 9: Amendment of Annexure A
 * Text: Annexure A amended by substitution of Forms 8, 10, 11, and 18.
Section 10: Short Title and Commencement
 * Text: Second Amendment of the Immigration Regulations, 2014; comes into operation on date of publication (20 May 2024).
